    {
      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To find the greatest common divisor (GCD) of 12 and 20, we will use the Euclidean algorithm. The Euclidean algorithm involves repeated division and taking remainders until we reach a remainder of 0. The last non-zero remainder is the GCD.\n\nHere are the steps:\n\n1. **Divide 20 by 12 and find the remainder:**\n   \\[\n   20 \\div 12 = 1 \\quad \\text{with a remainder of} \\quad 20 - 12 \\times 1 = 8\n   \\]\n   So, \\(20 = 12 \\times 1 + 8\\).\n\n2. **Now, divide 12 by 8 and find the remainder:**\n   \\[\n   12 \\div 8 = 1 \\quad \\text{with a remainder of} \\quad 12 - 8 \\times 1 = 4\n   \\]\n   So, \\(12 = 8 \\times 1 + 4\\).\n\n3. **Next, divide 8 by 4 and find the remainder:**\n   \\[\n   8 \\div 4 = 2 \\quad \\text{with a remainder of} \\quad 8 - 4 \\times 2 = 0\n   \\]\n   So, \\(8 = 4 \\times 2 + 0\\).\n\nSince the remainder is now 0, the last non-zero remainder is 4. Therefore, the greatest common divisor of 12 and 20 is \\(\\boxed{4}\\).",
